.\" Manpage for zosyazi
.\" Contact: https://github.com/
.TH ZOSYAZI 1 "20 November 2026" "zosyazi 1.1.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zosyazi \- lightweight terminal file manager for z/OS UNIX and /dsfs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zosyazi
[\fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-cwd\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zosyazi
is a zero-dependency, Yazi-inspired terminal file manager designed specifically for
\fBz/OS UNIX System Services (USS)\fR and the IBM Open Enterprise SDK for Python.
It features a 3-column Miller layout, Vim-style keybindings, Git branch/status badges,
and native awareness for \fBz/OS /dsfs (Data Set File System)\fR and \fBfile tags (ls \-T / chtag)\fR.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
Initial directory or file to open. Defaults to the current working directory (\fB.\fR).
Accepts absolute paths, relative paths, environment variables (e.g. \fI$HOME\fR),
and z/OS \fI/dsfs\fR paths (e.g. \fI/dsfs/txt/USER.*\fR).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd\-file= FILE
Write the final working directory to \fIFILE\fR upon exit. Useful for shell wrapper scripts to
automatically change the active shell directory to the directory browsed inside \fBzosyazi\fR.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the program's version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the command-line help message and exit.

.SH KEYBINDINGS

.SS Navigation
.TP
.BR j ", " Down
Move cursor down.
.TP
.BR k ", " Up
Move cursor up.
.TP
.BR h ", " H ", " Left ", " Backspace
Move directly to the parent directory.
.TP
.BR l ", " Right ", " Enter
Enter the highlighted directory or open the highlighted file in the built-in viewer.
.TP
.B v
Open the highlighted file directly in the built-in full-screen file viewer.
.TP
.BR g " / " G
Jump to the top / bottom of the directory listing.
.TP
.B c
Prompt for a new path to jump directly to (supports environment variables and \fI~\fR).
.TP
.B ~
Jump directly to the user's home directory.
.TP
.BR m\fIkey\fR " / " '\fIkey\fR
Set bookmark (\fBm\fR followed by a letter) or jump to bookmark (\fB'\fR followed by a letter).
Predefined bookmarks: \fBh\fR (home), \fBr\fR (/), \fBt\fR (/tmp), \fBd\fR (/dsfs/txt).
.TP
.BR / " then " Enter
Open the directory-name filter prompt. Press Enter to apply the filter or Escape to cancel.
The header displays the number of matches; Escape in the browser clears an active filter.
.TP
.B .
Toggle display of hidden files (dotfiles).

.SS File Operations
.TP
.B Space
Toggle selection mark on the highlighted item (supports multi-item operations); selected names
appear in the footer.
.TP
.BR y " / " x " / " p
Yank (copy) / Cut / Paste selected or highlighted items. The footer shows clipboard items and
the current paste destination. Existing destination items are skipped and reported.
.TP
.B d
Review the selected items or current item, then confirm deletion. Directories are removed
recursively; the confirmation screen marks them explicitly.
.TP
.B r
Rename the highlighted item.
.TP
.B a
Create a new file or directory (end the name with \fB/\fR to create a directory).
.TP
.B e
Open the highlighted file in \fB$EDITOR\fR (falls back to \fBvim\fR, \fBnano\fR, or \fBvi\fR).
Curses mode is cleanly suspended and restored.
.TP
.B T
Open the interactive z/OS file tagging prompt (\fBchtag\fR) to switch encoding
between ISO8859-1 (ASCII), IBM-1047 (EBCDIC), UTF-8, custom CCSID, or remove tagging.
.TP
.BR ! " or " X
Execute a shell command with the current item, or submit as a batch JCL job if the
file ends in \fI.jcl\fR, \fI.cntl\fR, or \fI.job\fR. In command prompts, \fB%f\fR is replaced
by the filename and \fB%F\fR is replaced by the full path.

.SS General
.TP
.B q
Quit \fBzosyazi\fR. Escape clears an active filter; otherwise it quits.
.TP
.BR F1 ", " ?
Toggle the interactive, color-coded help tutorial.

.SS Prompts
Prompts accept editable text, including input longer than the terminal width. Use Left / Right
or Home / End to move the cursor, Backspace / Delete to edit, and Ctrl-U to clear the input.
Press Enter to accept or Escape to cancel. The browser footer shows common navigation keys and
the help key.

.SH Z/OS & DSFS INTEGRATION
.B zosyazi
includes custom handling for z/OS specific concepts:
.IP \(bu 2
\fB/dsfs Awareness:\fR Prevents realpath resolution from breaking virtual HLQ directories
in \fI/dsfs/txt\fR, \fI/dsfs/bin\fR, and \fI/dsfs/rec\fR, and displays visual status popup
indicators when loading or navigating large datasets.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBHex & ASCII Dump:\fR Binary files and \fI/dsfs/bin\fR files are automatically rendered as
offset, hexadecimal, and ASCII representation in previews and the viewer.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEBCDIC / ASCII Decoding:\fR Files tagged as \fIIBM-1047\fR are decoded using \fIcp1047\fR,
while ASCII and UTF-8 files are decoded accordingly.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPerformance Caching:\fR Batch-fetches file tags across directories using \fIls \-T\fR to
eliminate per-item subprocess overhead on z/OS USS.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ZOSYAZI_DSFS
Root mount point for the Data Set File System (defaults to \fI/dsfs\fR).
.TP
.B EDITOR
Specifies the editor to use when pressing \fBe\fR.
.TP
.B HOME
Used for the home directory jump (\fB~\fR).

